            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is an [intended behavior](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/be81509b7160aa02264a59789164a2e1c4a6750a/doc/mini-extra.txt#L132). Forcing linewise mode (`gsVii`) is indeed one of the solutions here. The other is to use other indent textobject, like from 'mini.indentscope'.\n\n> The textobject provided by `mini.indentscope` works correctly, but I'm not a fan of the visual guides so I prefer to just use the one provided by `mini.extra`.\n\nIf it is the only thing that stops from using 'mini.indentscope', then drawing scope can be disabling by setting either `draw.delay = 10000000` or `draw.predicate = function() return false end` inside of `require('mini.indentscope').setup()`.",
